        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dprcooke/{size}/1961_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-02-27T18:53:10.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"TakeWalker\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/takewalker/48/5677_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> TakeWalker:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Yes, exactly that.And honestly, I think Setback would be less jealous and more, \"Gee, it's great Amanda has such a diversity of friends!\"</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I don't think Setback would be jealous, and <em>of course</em> he'd remain positive. &nbsp;But the whole point of the dinner date was to keep his sense of normalcy, so to have said dinner turn into the planning session for a warehouse raid with a well-known mercenary must, well, strain that sense of normalcy.</p>",
